      "content": "but there are no \"small things\" left. there's just this crushing weight of knowing i failed. every day i wake up and i just feel this immense exhaustion from trying to pretend that things might get better or that i can just \"be.\" it's like i'm a ghost haunted by the person i used to be. it feels like the most honest thing i could do is just stop. to just stop pretending and stop the struggle. it's just so much more exhausting than just... not being.",
